(Financial Decentralized Application - Project Report) Tj T*
(Prepared from the project source on 13 October 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Introduction) Tj T*
(Common Ground is a single-campaign Ethereum crowdfunding application. Its demonstration) Tj T*
(campaign, "The neighborhood learning room", presents a community space for reading, learning) Tj T*
(and sharing ideas. Contributors connect MetaMask and send test ETH to a Solidity contract. The) Tj T*
(contract holds funds until the campaign deadline and then permits either beneficiary) Tj T*
(withdrawal or individual refunds, depending on whether the funding goal was reached.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A decentralized application combines a conventional web interface with blockchain execution.) Tj T*
(Ethereum records transactions and runs the campaign rules; the browser provides a usable) Tj T*
(interface; Flask and SQLite maintain a convenient transaction-history index. The backend does) Tj T*
(not hold campaign funds or sign wallet transactions. This division makes the contract the) Tj T*
(authority for financial settlement while preserving familiar web application features.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Problem Statement) Tj T*
(Community fundraising requires contributors to trust that an organizer will apply the) Tj T*
(advertised funding conditions. If a campaign raises too little to proceed, returning) Tj T*
(contributions can require manual administration. Contributors also need clear evidence that) Tj T*
(their payments were recorded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This project addresses those concerns through an all-or-nothing funding rule enforced on-) Tj T*
(chain. Once deployed, the beneficiary, goal and deadline cannot be changed. Successful) Tj T*
(campaigns release funds only after the deadline; unsuccessful campaigns allow contributors to) Tj T*
(reclaim their recorded ETH. This guarantee concerns settlement conditions, rather than how the) Tj T*
(beneficiary spends funds after withdrawal. Gas fees remain the responsibility of each) Tj T*
(transaction sender.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Objectives) Tj T*
(- Implement an Ethereum contract for contributions, withdrawal and refunds.) Tj T*
(- Integrate MetaMask without collecting private keys or seed phrases.) Tj T*
(- Present live funding progress, campaign status and wallet contributions.) Tj T*
(- Verify transaction hashes independently before recording history.) Tj T*
(- Validate inputs and communicate wallet, network and service errors.) Tj T*
(- Provide automated test sources and repeatable deployment instructions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Scope and evidence) Tj T*
(This report describes the checked-in implementation and test sources. Automated tests were not) Tj T*
(executed for this report. Live Sepolia deployment, browser interactions, screenshots and) Tj T*
(performance measurements were not independently verified. The project is an educational) Tj T*
(demonstration using test ETH.) Tj T*
ET
