BT /F2 17 Tf 48 793 Td
(System Architecture and Technologies) Tj ET
0.16 0.16 0.16 rg
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 764 Td 10.5 TL
(4. System Architecture) Tj T*
(The application has four cooperating layers:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Browser UI -> MetaMask -> Ethereum RPC -> Crowdfund contract) Tj T*
(Browser UI -> Flask API -> independent Ethereum RPC verification) Tj T*
(Flask API -> SQLite transaction-history database) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The frontend reads campaign state through the wallet provider and requests a signature when a) Tj T*
(user contributes, withdraws or claims a refund. Ethereum executes the transaction. The browser) Tj T*
(then submits the transaction hash to Flask. Flask uses its own configured RPC provider to) Tj T*
(obtain authoritative transaction and receipt data, and stores the result in SQLite.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The separation matters because a database write cannot establish that ETH changed hands.) Tj T*
(Blockchain state determines the financial outcome. Conversely, a confirmed blockchain) Tj T*
(transaction remains valid even when the history service is unavailable. The interface retains) Tj T*
(unresolved hashes and retries indexing while the wallet is connected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The frontend and backend must use the same chain ID and deployed contract address. Local) Tj T*
(development uses chain ID 1337; the documented public-testnet workflow uses Sepolia, chain ID) Tj T*
(11155111. Wallet account and network changes reset the frontend session and require) Tj T*
(reconnection. Session checks reduce the chance of displaying asynchronous results for an) Tj T*
(outdated account.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Technologies Used) Tj T*
(- Next.js 16.3.7 and React 19.2.8: page composition and interactive UI.) Tj T*
(- TypeScript: typed campaign, wallet and transaction representations.) Tj T*
(- ethers.js 6: wallet provider, contract calls and exact ETH/wei conversion.) Tj T*
(- Solidity: immutable campaign rules and ETH custody.) Tj T*
(- Flask 3.1.2 and Web3.py 7.13.0: API and RPC verification.) Tj T*
(- SQLite: lightweight persistence of public transaction metadata.) Tj T*
(- Ganache: local blockchain development and contract test execution.) Tj T*
(- Docker Compose: coordinated frontend/backend deployment.) Tj T*
(- Gunicorn: production backend serving in the container configuration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Versions above reflect package declarations, rather than an independently inspected running) Tj T*
(deployment. The contract compiler script enables optimization with 200 runs and targets the) Tj T*
(Shanghai EVM. The Solidity source declares pragma ^0.8.30.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Technology rationale) Tj T*
(The stack separates presentation, verification and settlement into small components. SQLite is) Tj T*
(appropriate for a modest single-instance educational service. MetaMask provides user-) Tj T*
(controlled signing, while Solidity makes the campaign conditions inspectable and executable) Tj T*
(without relying on the Flask server to release funds.) Tj T*
ET
