0.12 0.21 0.28 rg
BT /F2 17 Tf 48 793 Td
(Smart Contract Design) Tj ET
0.16 0.16 0.16 rg
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 764 Td 10.5 TL
(6. Smart Contract Design) Tj T*
(The implementation is sol/Crowdfund.sol. Its constructor accepts a beneficiary address, target) Tj T*
(in wei and duration in seconds. It rejects a zero beneficiary, zero goal or zero duration. The) Tj T*
(deadline is calculated from the deployment block timestamp. Beneficiary, goal and deadline are) Tj T*
(immutable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(State includes totalRaised, withdrawn and a contributions mapping keyed by wallet address.) Tj T*
(totalRaised represents cumulative historical contributions, rather than the remaining ETH) Tj T*
(balance. It is deliberately not reduced after settlement. A wallet's contribution is reset to) Tj T*
(zero when its refund succeeds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Contribution) Tj T*
(contribute\(\) is payable. It accepts positive ETH only when block.timestamp is strictly before) Tj T*
(the deadline. It increases the sender's contribution and totalRaised, then emits Contributed.) Tj T*
(Overfunding is allowed; reaching the goal early does not end the campaign or unlock early) Tj T*
(withdrawal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Successful settlement) Tj T*
(withdraw\(\) requires the caller to be the beneficiary, the deadline to have passed, totalRaised) Tj T*
(to meet the goal and withdrawn to be false. It marks the campaign withdrawn before) Tj T*
(transferring the entire contract balance to the beneficiary. A failed transfer reverts the) Tj T*
(transaction, including the state update. Withdrawn records the recipient and amount.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Unsuccessful settlement) Tj T*
(refund\(\) requires the deadline to have passed and totalRaised to remain below the goal. The) Tj T*
(caller must have a positive recorded contribution. The function clears that contribution) Tj T*
(before transferring its value back and emits Refunded. Contributors claim individually; the) Tj T*
(contract does not loop over all donors. A second successful refund from the same contribution) Tj T*
(is prevented.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Security and gas considerations) Tj T*
(Authorization depends on msg.sender, not a frontend-supplied identity. Outgoing transfers) Tj T*
(follow checks-effects-interactions: settlement eligibility is checked and state updated before) Tj T*
(external calls. These choices address repeat settlement and basic reentrancy concerns, but do) Tj T*
(not constitute a comprehensive audit. Ordinary direct ETH transfers without a supported) Tj T*
(payable function are rejected because no receive or fallback handler is defined.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Immutable campaign parameters reduce administrative discretion. Per-wallet refunds avoid a) Tj T*
(settlement loop whose gas cost grows with donor count. Compiler optimization is enabled, but) Tj T*
(gas savings were not measured. ETH amounts use integer wei, avoiding floating-point accounting) Tj T*
(errors. The application never promises that network fees are refundable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(State transitions) Tj T*
(Active -> deadline reached -> goal met -> beneficiary withdraws once.) Tj T*
(Active -> deadline reached -> goal missed -> each donor claims a refund.) Tj T*
(No contract path changes the campaign goal or extends the deadline.) Tj T*
ET
