0.12 0.21 0.28 rg
BT /F2 17 Tf 48 793 Td
(Application Design and Implementation) Tj ET
0.16 0.16 0.16 rg
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 764 Td 10.5 TL
(7. Application Design) Tj T*
(The interface combines a campaign story, funding panel and transaction history. The story) Tj T*
(explains the community purpose and settlement promise. The funding panel shows ETH raised,) Tj T*
(goal, percentage funded, deadline and the connected wallet's contribution. It supports manual) Tj T*
(amounts and preset contributions of 0.01, 0.05 and 0.1 ETH.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Buttons reflect the campaign state. Contributions close after the deadline. Refunds appear for) Tj T*
(eligible contributors when the goal was missed. Withdrawal appears for the beneficiary after a) Tj T*
(successful campaign ends. These controls help users choose valid actions, while the contract) Tj T*
(remains responsible for enforcing permissions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Implementation) Tj T*
(frontend/src/hooks/use-campaign.ts coordinates wallet connection, contract reads, transaction) Tj T*
(submission and history reconciliation. It reads beneficiary, goal, total raised, deadline,) Tj T*
(withdrawn status, the user's contribution and the latest block. Settlement availability is) Tj T*
(based on blockchain time. A 12-second refresh interval updates campaign and history data while) Tj T*
(connected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Before submission, the frontend checks the configured network, selected signer and presence of) Tj T*
(contract code at the address. contributionWei\(\) accepts a positive decimal ETH amount with at) Tj T*
(most 18 decimal places and converts it to bigint wei through ethers. Invalid, zero, negative) Tj T*
(and over-precision amounts are rejected. Wallet rejection receives an actionable message.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After broadcasting, the UI exposes the transaction hash, attempts history indexing and waits) Tj T*
(for one block confirmation with a 120-second timeout. An error after broadcast prompts the) Tj T*
(user to check the hash before retrying. This distinction helps prevent duplicate contributions) Tj T*
(caused by confusing an indexing failure with a payment failure.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Backend verification) Tj T*
(POST /api/transactions accepts a syntactically valid transaction hash. Flask checks the RPC) Tj T*
(chain ID, recipient contract and exact four-byte selector for contribute\(\), refund\(\) or) Tj T*
(withdraw\(\). Sender, ETH value and receipt status come from RPC, rather than client claims.) Tj T*
(Unknown transactions return 404, invalid or unrelated requests return 400, and) Tj T*
(configuration/provider failures return 503.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GET /api/transactions?wallet=... returns up to 100 indexed records for the wallet, configured) Tj T*
(chain and contract. GET /api/health reports service liveness. CORS allows the configured web) Tj T*
(origin; incoming request bodies are limited to 2,048 bytes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SQLite stores hash, chain ID, contract address, wallet, action, transaction value in wei,) Tj T*
(status, block number and creation timestamp. The primary key is \(chain_id, hash\), enabling) Tj T*
(idempotent status updates. Transaction value is stored as text; for withdrawal/refund calls,) Tj T*
(this is the call's attached ETH value, not the contract's outgoing settlement amount.) Tj T*
ET
