0.12 0.21 0.28 rg
BT /F2 17 Tf 48 793 Td
(Evaluation, Challenges and Limitations) Tj ET
0.16 0.16 0.16 rg
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 764 Td 10.5 TL
(10. Challenges Encountered) Tj T*
(The code reveals several integration challenges and the strategies used to address them. These) Tj T*
(observations describe implementation choices; they are not a reconstructed development diary.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Exact currency handling: JavaScript floating-point arithmetic is unsuitable for wei) Tj T*
(accounting. The project uses decimal validation and bigint conversion, preserving up to 18 ETH) Tj T*
(decimal places.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Wallet and network consistency: users can change accounts or chains during asynchronous) Tj T*
(requests. Event handlers reset the session, and submission checks confirm the expected signer) Tj T*
(and network. Users reconnect to reload the campaign.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Blockchain/API consistency: a transaction can be broadcast before the server RPC sees it, or) Tj T*
(can succeed while Flask is unavailable. The frontend saves unresolved hashes locally and) Tj T*
(retries indexing. The backend accepts repeated submissions idempotently and derives status) Tj T*
(from receipts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Deployment consistency: the wallet and server use separate RPC access, and frontend) Tj T*
(configuration is fixed during the build. Documentation emphasizes matching chain/address) Tj T*
(settings and rebuilding after public configuration changes. Persistent volumes or disks) Tj T*
(preserve SQLite history across container replacement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(11. Limitations) Tj T*
(Only one configured campaign is presented at a time. The story is a demonstration, and there) Tj T*
(is no campaign directory, creation interface, organizer verification or milestone-based) Tj T*
(release. The contract controls funding conditions but cannot verify whether a beneficiary) Tj T*
(delivers the promised community project.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(History is an index of submitted hashes, not a complete blockchain scan. Transactions made) Tj T*
(outside the app need explicit indexing. History responses are limited to 100 rows. Receipt) Tj T*
(status is refreshed through POST reconciliation, rather than by the GET endpoint itself.) Tj T*
(Clearing browser storage can remove unresolved hashes unless the user preserves them) Tj T*
(elsewhere.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One mined receipt is treated as confirmed, not finalized. Chain reorganizations, replaced) Tj T*
(transactions and dropped transactions require additional reconciliation. The application has) Tj T*
(no background indexer, measured load capacity or independently audited contract. No rate-) Tj T*
(limiting layer is implemented.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Security, privacy and performance evaluation) Tj T*
(MetaMask protects signing keys from the application. Public wallet addresses and transaction) Tj T*
(metadata remain visible; pseudonymous addresses should not be described as anonymous) Tj T*
(identities. CORS restricts browser origins but is not authentication. The API intentionally) Tj T*
(permits anyone to index an existing public campaign transaction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Twelve-second polling, 10-second backend RPC timeouts and 12-second frontend API timeouts are) Tj T*
(configuration choices, not measured response-time results. Gas costs, usability outcomes and) Tj T*
(end-to-end latency have not been benchmarked. SQLite and a single-instance backend suit the) Tj T*
(current scale but need reassessment for broader deployment.) Tj T*
ET
