0.12 0.21 0.28 rg
BT /F2 17 Tf 48 793 Td
(Future Improvements and Conclusion) Tj ET
0.16 0.16 0.16 rg
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 764 Td 10.5 TL
(12. Future Improvements) Tj T*
(First, strengthen evidence and operational confidence. Execute the supplied tests and record) Tj T*
(their outputs, then perform the complete MetaMask/Sepolia walkthrough. Add real screenshots) Tj T*
(and deployment transaction references to the submission. Measure confirmation latency, API) Tj T*
(response times and gas costs across contribution, withdrawal and refund scenarios.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Second, improve reconciliation. A background event indexer could discover transactions) Tj T*
(independently of browser submissions and update receipt status. Confirmation-depth tracking,) Tj T*
(reorganization handling and replacement-transaction detection would provide more reliable) Tj T*
(status semantics. Pagination would remove the 100-record history ceiling.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Third, expand the product carefully. A campaign factory and directory could support multiple) Tj T*
(campaigns, with explicit organizer information and configurable campaign narratives. Any) Tj T*
(milestone release or beneficiary governance feature would require a revised contract design) Tj T*
(and new financial-rule tests. Independent security review should precede use with real funds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Fourth, strengthen hosting and accessibility. Add database backups, API rate limits,) Tj T*
(monitoring and RPC failure alerts. Evaluate keyboard navigation, screen-reader output, smaller) Tj T*
(displays and wallet flows with users. Public deployment should use HTTPS and maintain durable) Tj T*
(storage. Additional automated tests should target failed transfers, adversarial receiver) Tj T*
(contracts and recovery under network interruption.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(13. Conclusion) Tj T*
(Common Ground implements the central elements of a financial DApp: a Solidity contract,) Tj T*
(MetaMask connection, ETH transactions, a web interface, a Flask backend and transaction-) Tj T*
(history persistence. Its all-or-nothing model makes the settlement conditions explicit and) Tj T*
(enforces them on Ethereum. Contributors can fund a campaign before its deadline; afterward,) Tj T*
(successful campaigns allow beneficiary withdrawal and unsuccessful campaigns allow individual) Tj T*
(refunds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The design keeps financial authority on-chain and uses the backend as a verified public-data) Tj T*
(index. Integer currency handling, immutable campaign parameters and state updates before) Tj T*
(outgoing transfers provide a sound educational foundation. The main remaining work is) Tj T*
(demonstrated test execution, live wallet evidence and stronger indexing and operational) Tj T*
(controls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source basis) Tj T*
(This report was prepared from doc/assignment.docx, README.md, sol/Crowdfund.sol,) Tj T*
(frontend/package.json, frontend/src/hooks/use-campaign.ts, frontend/src/lib/,) Tj T*
(frontend/src/components/, frontend/scripts/compile.mjs, frontend/tests/, backend/src/,) Tj T*
(backend/tests/test_app.py, compose.yaml and render.yaml. These local sources support the) Tj T*
(implementation claims; external documentation and live deployment state were not independently) Tj T*
(verified.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Submission note) Tj T*
(The PDF contains seven pages and follows all thirteen report sections requested by the) Tj T*
(assignment. Student identity details, real execution screenshots and the separate 5-8 minute) Tj T*
(demonstration video should be supplied by the author. This report does not claim those) Tj T*
(artifacts already exist.) Tj T*
